CDEPS: reuse identical stream route handles instead of rebuilding per stream

APPLIES ON TOP OF cdeps-strdata-timers.patch. The trace regions it adds are also
how this change is verified: the Count column of strdata_regridstore falls from
the stream count to the number of distinct route handles.

shr_strdata_init called ESMF_FieldRegridStore once per stream, unconditionally.
That call generates interpolation weights; for a large model mesh it dominates
data model initialisation, and a configuration whose streams share a source mesh
and a mapalgo pays the whole cost again for every stream.

Measured on ACCESS-OM3 at 8 km, 8216 PETs:

  datm_strdata_init                  1   118.5573
    strdata_streamloop               1   113.0859   95.4%
      strdata_regridstore            9   112.5007   94.9%   <- 12.50 s per stream
      strdata_streammesh             9     0.5656    0.5%
      strdata_fldbun                 9     0.0106    0.0%
    strdata_modelmesh                1     5.2561    4.4%
    strdata_readxml                  1     0.2097    0.2%

That configuration has 9 DATM streams which all name the same
JRA55do-datm-ESMFmesh.nc, all regrid to the same 4320x3672 model mesh, and use
two distinct mapalgo values (consf x4, patch x5). Two route handles are needed;
nine were built. DROF repeats it smaller: 2 streams, both consd, one mesh.
Collapsing 9 -> 2 and 2 -> 1 should return about 89 s, roughly 10% of a 1-day
benchmark for this configuration and about 1% of a 1-month production segment.

Why the reuse is sound: a route handle depends on the source geometry, the
destination geometry and the regrid options, not on the particular fields passed
to the store call, so it is valid for any later ESMF_FieldRegrid between fields
of the same geometry. This routine already relies on that -- the handle built
from field_stream is used at shr_strdata_advance with field_stream_vector, which
carries an extra ungridded dimension.

The scan never leaves one sdat, so the destination mesh and the VM are the same
by construction. What must match is the stream mesh file name, stream_nlev (it
decides whether field_stream has an ungridded dimension), the mapalgo string
(which also carries the weight file path for mapfile:), and src_mask_val and
dst_mask_val, both of which are passed to ESMF_FieldRegridStore.

Nothing in CDEPS destroys sdat%pstrm(:)%routehandle, so sharing introduces no
double-free today. routehandle_isowner records which stream built the handle so
a future ESMF_RouteHandleDestroy can be added safely; routehandle_created marks
entries usable at all -- streams with mapalgo 'none' are neither cached nor
reused. Every decision is written to the component log.

Touches mediator-side nothing; only streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90.

diff --git a/streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90 b/streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90
index 814cbcc..64147d2 100644
--- a/streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90
+++ b/streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@ module dshr_strdata_mod
      type(io_desc_t)                     :: stream_pio_iodesc               ! stream pio descriptor
      logical                             :: stream_pio_iodesc_set =.false.  ! true=>pio iodesc has been set
      type(ESMF_RouteHandle)              :: routehandle                     ! stream n -> model mesh mapping
+     logical                             :: routehandle_created = .false.   ! true => routehandle is usable
+     logical                             :: routehandle_isowner = .false.   ! false => shared from an earlier
+                                                                            ! stream; do not destroy via this
+                                                                            ! stream
      character(len=CL), allocatable      :: fldlist_stream(:)               ! names of stream file fields
      character(len=CL), allocatable      :: fldlist_model(:)                ! names of stream model fields
      integer                             :: stream_nlev                     ! number of vertical levels in stream
@@ -477,6 +481,8 @@ contains
     type(ESMF_VM)                :: vm
     integer                      :: nvars
     integer                      :: i, stream_nlev, index, istat
+    integer                      :: ns_rh, i_rh     ! route handle reuse: match index, scan index
+    character(len=CX)            :: filename_cmp    ! mesh file of the stream being compared against
     character(len=CL)            :: stream_vector_names
     character(len=CL)            :: mapfile
     character(len=*), parameter  :: subname='(shr_sdat_init)'
@@ -656,7 +662,46 @@ contains
        if (.not.  ESMF_MeshIsCreated(stream_mesh)) then
           sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo = 'none'
        else
-          if (trim(sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo) == "bilinear") then
+          ! Reuse an identical route handle from an earlier stream rather than building
+          ! another one. ESMF_FieldRegridStore generates interpolation weights, and for a
+          ! large model mesh that dominates data model initialisation; configurations
+          ! whose streams share a source mesh and a mapalgo pay for it once per stream.
+          !
+          ! A route handle depends on the source geometry, the destination geometry and
+          ! the regrid options, not on the particular fields handed to the store call, so
+          ! it is valid for any later ESMF_FieldRegrid between fields of the same geometry.
+          ! This routine already relies on that: the handle built below from field_stream
+          ! is used with field_stream_vector, which carries an extra ungridded dimension.
+          !
+          ! The destination is sdat%model_mesh and the search is confined to this sdat, so
+          ! the destination geometry and the VM are the same by construction. What must
+          ! match is the source mesh file, the number of stream levels (it decides whether
+          ! field_stream carries an ungridded dimension), the mapalgo string (which also
+          ! carries the weight file path in the mapfile: case) and both mask values.
+          ns_rh = 0
+          do i_rh = 1, ns-1
+             if (.not. sdat%pstrm(i_rh)%routehandle_created)                      cycle
+             if (sdat%pstrm(i_rh)%stream_nlev /= stream_nlev)                     cycle
+             if (trim(sdat%stream(i_rh)%mapalgo) /= trim(sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo)) cycle
+             if (sdat%stream(i_rh)%src_mask_val /= sdat%stream(ns)%src_mask_val)  cycle
+             if (sdat%stream(i_rh)%dst_mask_val /= sdat%stream(ns)%dst_mask_val)  cycle
+             call shr_stream_getMeshFileName(sdat%stream(i_rh), filename_cmp)
+             if (trim(filename_cmp) /= trim(filename))                            cycle
+             ns_rh = i_rh
+             exit
+          end do
+
+          if (ns_rh > 0) then
+             sdat%pstrm(ns)%routehandle         = sdat%pstrm(ns_rh)%routehandle
+             sdat%pstrm(ns)%routehandle_created = .true.
+             sdat%pstrm(ns)%routehandle_isowner = .false.
+             if (sdat%mainproc) then
+                write(sdat%logunit,'(a,i0,a,i0,4a)') subname//' stream ',ns, &
+                     ' reuses the route handle built for stream ',ns_rh, &
+                     ', mapalgo ',trim(sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo), &
+                     ', mesh ',trim(filename)
+             end if
+          else if (trim(sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo) == "bilinear") then
              call ESMF_FieldRegridStore(sdat%pstrm(ns)%field_stream, lfield_dst, &
                   routehandle=sdat%pstrm(ns)%routehandle, &
                   regridmethod=ESMF_REGRIDMETHOD_BILINEAR,  &
@@ -720,6 +765,15 @@ contains
              call shr_log_error('ERROR: map algo '//trim(sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo)//' is not supported', rc=rc)
              return
           end if
+          if (ns_rh == 0 .and. trim(sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo) /= 'none') then
+             sdat%pstrm(ns)%routehandle_created = .true.
+             sdat%pstrm(ns)%routehandle_isowner = .true.
+             if (sdat%mainproc) then
+                write(sdat%logunit,'(a,i0,4a)') subname//' stream ',ns, &
+                     ' built a route handle, mapalgo ',trim(sdat%stream(ns)%mapalgo), &
+                     ', mesh ',trim(filename)
+             end if
+          end if
        end if
        call ESMF_TraceRegionExit('strdata_regridstore')
 
